From: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
Date: Sat, 26 Sep 2026 15:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] AP MLD: block a scan only while a partner link scans

hostapd_driver_scan() refuses a scan with -EBUSY while a partner link
of the same AP MLD is in HAPD_IFACE_ACS. A link stays in that state
while it waits to retry a refused scan. When two links start ACS at the
same time, the second one is refused, and from then on each link finds
the other in HAPD_IFACE_ACS on every retry. Neither link scans again,
and both give up after ACS_SCAN_RETRY_MAX_COUNT attempts.

The check exists because scan results without a matching scan cookie
go to the link that received the event, or to a partner link with a
scan callback. That needs at most one partner with a scan outstanding,
not at most one partner in ACS. Test for the scan callback instead of
the interface state. This also covers the HT 20/40 coexistence scan,
which sets the scan callback as well.

Fixes: 76f8cfd6a206 ("AP MLD: Fix ACS and HT scan related issues")
Signed-off-by: Felix Fietkau <nbd@nbd.name>
---
--- a/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
+++ b/src/ap/ap_drv_ops.c
@@ -799,9 +799,9 @@ int hostapd_driver_scan(struct hostapd_d
 			h_hapd = h_iface->bss[0];
 
 			if (hostapd_is_ml_partner(hapd, h_hapd) &&
-			    h_hapd->iface->state == HAPD_IFACE_ACS) {
+			    h_iface->scan_cb) {
 				wpa_printf(MSG_INFO,
-					   "ACS in progress in a partner link - try to scan later");
+					   "Scan in progress in a partner link - try to scan later");
 				return -EBUSY;
 			}
 		}
